WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.910
Over the past several months, there has been
an influx of so called moonbois within reddit,

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:10.380
stocktwits, the YouTube comments, and basically
every other medium of online communication.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.210
For the first time in history, bad news is
good news.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.190
In fact, the worse the news, the better.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.869
Is a company accused of fraud?

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:20.500
It’s time to buy.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.460
Is a company massively shorted and in a dying
industry?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.289
It’s time to buy.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:27.699
Is a company or a crypto a popular meme?

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:33.130
Well, you know the deal, it’s time to buy
the dip and take this trash to the moon.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.870
The worst part is that recent market conditions
have rewarded such behavior prompting these

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.930
individuals to continuously gamble their gains
on quote on quote the next short squeeze or

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.450
the next doge coin.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:49.100
And honestly, if they don’t take profits
and stop while they can, they’re portfolio

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.010
is going to end up being the next bitconnect.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:56.420
So, here’s the appallingly toxic culture
of moonbois.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.680
Before we get started, I wanted to make it
clear that I agree that hedge funds and market

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.120
makers are evil.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.780
They manipulate markets, they manipulate news,
and they manipulate emotions.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.970
Really, there’s nothing that they don’t
manipulate.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:14.439
But, yoloing one’s entire money on a nameless
penny stock or altcoin is not the solution.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:18.580
In fact, you’re probably increasing the
likelihood of handing over everything to the

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.110
big bois and here’s why.

00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:23.710
First of all, moonbois are cherry picking
favorable results.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.710
Gamestop was a magnificent short squeeze.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.130
People who got in early and took profits were
often able to profit hundreds of thousands

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.950
if not millions of dollars.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:34.360
But GameStop was a 1 in 10 million or a 1
in 100 million outcome.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.049
You could argue that Tesla’s run up was
also a massive short squeeze, but there were

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:41.920
many more factors hyping up Tesla’s run
than a simple technical short squeeze.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:46.200
Really, the last time a spectacular short
squeeze happened was with Volkswagen way back

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.240
in 2008.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.140
And, no retail investors were really involved
in that short squeeze.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:54.850
But, you don’t even have to look that far
to understand the low probability of such

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.590
a short squeeze.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.020
Gamestop is one of the most popular events
of 2021.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.009
Even people who have never invested in their
entire life have heard about the gamestop

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:05.009
story.

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:08.340
Considering this, don’t you think hedge
funds and market makers who work on wall street

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.690
all day every day know about it as well?

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.430
Wouldn’t it make sense that they would be
far more careful now that they took a massive

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.430
loss.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.620
I mean, it sounds like common sense, yet we
see new short squeeze opportunities posted

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.099
on reddit and stocktwits on a daily basis.

00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:26.400
Whether that be Microvision or Nikola or Blink
or AMC.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.420
Basically any stock that’s down 70 or 80%
and has a massive short interest is a new

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.870
short squeeze target.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.090
I mean if you want to throw 1 or 2% of your
portfolio into one of these companies just

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.090
for the fun of it.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.530
Go right ahead.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.400
But, moonbois are often taking out lines of
credit on their homes, maxing out their credit

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.080
cards, and throwing everything they have on
some pipe dream short squeeze.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.410
The worst part though is that they often convince
new and naive investors who have no idea what’s

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.890
happening to do the exact same thing.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.680
Is it going to work for someone?

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.680
Yes.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.420
But someone is also always going to win the
lottery.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.460
Anyway, moving away from short squeeze moonbois,
we have altcoin moonbois.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:07.000
Here, it’s basically the same thing, but
even worse.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.730
Instead of pointing to gamestop, altcoin moonbois
point to dogecoin.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.780
They claim that worthless altcoins like safemoon
coin and shiba coin and deeznuts coin are

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.470
going to the moon.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.870
And yes, there’s actually an altcoin called
deeznuts coin.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.459
The reason altcoin moonbois are even worse
is that the only people they’re screwing

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:26.299
over are their peers.

00:03:26.299 --> 00:03:30.159
With short squeezes, the people who are hurt
the most are also usually just retailers who

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:31.159
got in late.

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:35.440
But, there’s atleast a chance that hedge
funds and market makers could get hurt.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:40.489
With these nameless altcoins though, the only
person getting hurt is retailers, as no institution

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:43.310
is going to touch these worthless pieces of
garbage.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:48.220
With altcoins, scummy individuals are literally
running pump and dumps in broad daylight.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.890
Are there naive moonbois involved in these
schemes that don’t know exactly what they’re

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:52.890
doing?

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:53.890
Probably.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.650
But the people at the top of these pyramids
know exactly what they’re doing.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.690
All they’re doing is hyping up coins to
inflate the price, so that they can dump at

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:01.690
the top.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:05.600
I mean this is literally what the Wolf of
Wall Street did with penny stocks and it landed

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.910
him 2 years in federal prison.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.489
The altcoin ponzi leaders are straight up
committing fraud and theft in broad daylight,

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:15.860
but since cryptocurrencies aren’t regulated,
they can get away with it.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.030
It’s really quite disgusting.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:22.520
Aside from selling pipedreams to new investors,
moonbois are constantly normailizng ludicrous

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.660
losses on reddit and stocktwits.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.990
We’re talking 70 80 even 90% losses.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.130
And it’s not like they put in $100 and lost
$80.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:36.800
No, these guys put in hundreds of thousands
of dollars and then often lose hundreds of

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.889
thousands.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:42.970
Take a look at this wallstreetbets poster,
he lost $212,000.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.250
This guy lost $95,000.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.430
And this guy lost $589,000.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:54.020
On WallStreetBets and stocktwits, these aren’t
warnings to stay away or stories of people

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.370
learning their lessons.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.300
No, these are proud battle scars.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.110
Most of these gamblers think that they’re
a brave soldier holding the line and that

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.480
they’re going to be rewarded massively when
the short squeeze finally begins.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:10.830
In the future, they think that this loss will
be a funny story that they can laugh about.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.830
Maybe in a year they can post a new story
that's like, Oh yeah, I was down half a mil

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.950
last year, but now, I’m up 10 mil.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:22.340
In reality though, the only thing that's gonna
be funny at the end of the day is their final

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.180
account value after they blew a 100% because
of pure stupidity.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:32.710
I feel bad for people who randomly get screwed
out of nowhere, but these guys, man, they’re

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.260
just asking for it.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:39.130
They take pride in holding massive bags and
having what they call diamond hands.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.040
Diamond hands are awesome if you invested
into a fundamentally strong company that’s

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.040
vastly undervalued.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:49.270
But these guys are buying into pure hype and
are hoping that things get even more heated.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:54.700
Sometimes, this strategy even works, but instead
of taking profits along the way they end up

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.440
losing most of their gains.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:02.570
This poster for instance started from $10,000
and skyrocketed all the way to $1.6 million.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:07.610
He could’ve taken profits right then and
there, but he ended up riding it down to $250,000.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:12.930
Granted, he did still 25x his money, but that’s
still such a sad story.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.630
Imagine if he just sold 10% of his position
for every $100k he made.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:20.680
Or what if he just put a stop loss at $1 million.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:25.280
If you’re so confident in your thesis, putting
in a stop loss wouldn’t matter right?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.690
The stop loss should theoretically never hit.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:32.580
But, on the off chance it did hit, you would
guarantee yourself $1 million pre tax.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:37.069
Unfortunately though, that would be classified
as having paper hands and that’s a big no

00:06:37.069 --> 00:06:39.000
no amongst these communities.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.660
Risk management and smart trading tactics
are for losers, here, it’s either ride or

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.780
die with diamond hands.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.460
Not only do these communities encourage people
to not sell until some fairytale number is

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.850
reached, but they also promote infinitely
buying the dip.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.850
Again, buying the dip is a great strategy
when you’re investing into fundamentally

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.599
sound companies like Amazon or Apple.

00:06:59.599 --> 00:07:04.280
But, moonbois aren’t buying dips, they’re
buying crashes and falling knives.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.870
There’s always some random hype that gets
circulated amongst these communities that’s

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.050
gonna be game changing for the asset.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:15.210
You might hear that the institutions are trying
to buy your shares at cheap prices or that

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:18.870
they’re trying to shake out the weak hands
and that the pump is just around the corner.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.669
Check out this gambler for instance.

00:07:20.669 --> 00:07:25.910
His thesis is that the IV or implied volatility
of Gamestop options is under 100%.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.460
The company also has earnings and a shareholder
meeting coming soon.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:36.289
So, this user decided to go ahead and buy
nearly a $100k worth of $950 call options

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.630
on Gamestop.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:41.520
For those of you who aren’t familiar with
call options, this position basically means

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:48.400
that this user is betting $100k that Gamsetop
will be above $950 per share by January of

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.400
2023.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.750
At least, he bought something with 1.5 years
to play out, but man talk about risk management.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.699
Now, none of this is anything new.

00:07:57.699 --> 00:08:01.330
People have been using the stock market as
a casino for decades at this point.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.449
But with the success of Gamestop and Dogecoin,
more regular people are falling into this

00:08:05.449 --> 00:08:07.430
trap than ever before.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.889
These people simply don’t understand the
risks of investing into short squeeze stocks

00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:14.389
and hype cryptos.

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:21.190
They’re being sold a fantasy from moonbois
who either don’t understand the risk themselves

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:23.170
or they’re braindead gamblers.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:27.970
And unfortunately, the vast majority of these
individuals will end up losing everything.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:32.219
Anyone who tries to argue against these moonbois
or anyone who even tries to simply outline

00:08:32.219 --> 00:08:35.789
the risks of such activities are labeled as
gay bears.

00:08:35.789 --> 00:08:39.520
There’s gonna be comments down below that
I’m paid by hedge funds to spread fear,

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.830
uncertainty, and doubt and that I’m a tool
for big money.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.399
But in reality, the real tool for big money
is moon bois.

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:52.500
And that brings me into my last point which
is that there is no larger mission.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:56.000
Oftentimes, wall street betters and moon bois
think that they’re doing something super

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.089
noble by taking down big money and helping
the little guy win.

00:09:00.089 --> 00:09:03.490
Even with gamestop, the little guy didn’t
win.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:09.860
Sure, some retailers won, but retail investors
as a whole did not win by any means.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:13.910
Moonbois were super excited that the hedge
fund melvin capital lost 53% of their portfolio

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:14.970
in January.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:20.029
But, what people don’t mention is that melvin
capital gained 20% the very next month, and

00:09:20.029 --> 00:09:23.540
at that rate, they’ll probably be green
by the end of the year.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.660
Now, you might be saying that Robinhood and
the other brokerages came to their rescue,

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:31.350
and that they would’ve gone under if it
wasn’t for interference.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:35.830
But even if Melvin capital and citron research
went bankrupt, who cares?

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:40.460
That’s just a handful of hedge funds, and
hedge funds would’ve still won the gamestop

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:45.320
fiasco even if GameStop went to the moon and
hit $2000 or $3000 per share.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:50.470
Here’s the thing, hedge funds don’t just
short stocks, they also buy stocks just like

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:51.470
retailers.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:57.140
In fact, the four largest asset managers in
the world own a total of 39% of Gamestop.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:01.560
Aside from these hedge funds who already owned
gamestop, dozens of hedge funds got in and

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.360
got out of gamestop just like you.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:07.280
And they made a lot lot more.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:12.160
Even DFV, who is likely the retailer that
benefited the most, only made 30 or maybe

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.600
$40 million at the peak which is of course
insane.

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:19.390
But, a hedge fund named Senvest management
that decided to jump into the Gamestop frenzy

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.690
ended up pocketing $700 million.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:26.890
If Robinhood didn’t shut down gamestop stock
buying, not only would retailers have made

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:31.230
millions more, but hedge funds on the right
side of the trade would have made billions

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.230
more.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.850
So, it’s really not as noble of a fight
as you might think.

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:40.820
At the end of the day, the stock and crypto
markets have skyrocketed over the past year.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:45.230
The PE ratio of the S&amp;P 500 would suggest
that we’re actually at dotcom bubble levels

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.510
right now.

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:49.880
This massive speculation across the stock
market has allowed a group of moonbois on

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:55.760
reddit, stocktwits, and youtube to make unprecedented
returns within a very short period of time.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.660
This short term victory has led them to believe
that they can replicate these results over

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:03.720
and over again adding a zero to their portfolio
with each subsequent win.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:08.510
But, sooner or later the house of cards will
crumble and most of them will lose everything

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.480
just like every other euphoric event in history.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.730
So, be sure that you’re not the one that's
diamond handing to 0.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.529
What do you guys think about moonbois?

00:11:17.529 --> 00:11:18.650
Comment that down below.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:23.260
Also, drop a like if you guys think this market
is in need of some reason and logic.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.970
And of course, consider joining our discord
community to suggest future video ideas and

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:31.420
consider subscribing to see more questions
logically answered.

